 "contract": "attendance/src/attendance/acp_view.py, GET /families/{family}/sessions",
 "entry": "noticeboard.sessions.SessionReader.sessions",
 "format": 1,
 "notes": ["The input is the bytes of the body of one answer of attendance. params.status is the HTTP status of that answer.","params.family and params.cursor are the arguments of the entry point. An empty cursor is the default, and the reader then sends no cursor.","value.request is the call that the reader makes: the path, and each parameter of the query as text. The reader sends its token in a header and never in the query.","value.rows is each session of the answer. family is the family of the call. origin is what started the session: the kind and the name of the trigger, then delegation, then job. It is empty for a session with none of the three.","The reader takes the first 200 items of the list and then drops each item that is no object.","A field of a wrong type reads as an empty text, as 0, as false or as absent. A text has 500 characters or less. A character is one code point.","A refused vector is an answer that the reader gets nothing from. refusal is the problem that a page shows.","The vector transport-problem has no answer: args.problem is the text that the transport gives the reader in the place of one. The reader gives a page the same text.","A problem is an object. class is one of none, missing, unreadable, too large, not JSON, not an object, refused, unreachable, not a record and capped. capped is a notice: the reader stopped at a limit and kept what it read before.","text is the sentence that a page shows. A problem of the class not JSON has no text: its sentence ends with a message of the JSON reader of Python. It has start, the part of the sentence before that message."],
